star citizen director chris roberts has  responded to criticisms about the  lengthy development of the game which  kicked off with a fundraising campaign  in 2012 that has since raised 132  million bucks and count the game has  still not been fully released the  initial target release dates have come  and gone due to the game growing in size  and scope in a candid blog post robert  said that cloud Imperium games have  decided to now share target dates that  are subject to change and will be  transparent about their development  schedule and progress he explains that  target dates are not release dates and  everything you see will shift at some  point sometime sightly and sometimes  wildly the danger in doing that has been  that casual observers will not  understand this that there'll be an  outcry that delays every time we update  the page while that is a risk above all  we trust the community that has given us  so much support beginning with star  citizen alpha 2.6 cloud Imperium will be  sharing their internal development  schedule on a weekly basis as a  permanent fixture on the Roberts space  industries websites Roberts added the  simple fact is that game development  especially game development on the scale  of star citizen is complicated if you  talk to any developer that works on  large titles they will tell you that  schedules especially earlier in the  development cycle move all the time most  people never see this because the  publisher won't announce a project  publicly until it's very far along for  the full blog post and updates on the  progress of star citizen check out our  story on GameSpot
 

